commit(n,t,ds,ch,items,'The page reduces preservation of divided powers of sums to summands, then studies monomials and generators of a pd ideal J inside A mapping to K inside B. It explicitly asks two displayed equalities with a question mark. The word after pour les remains sommants|sommands, not H’s monômes. The long single strokes between first and last factors are retained literally; in the argument they serve as product continuation, not subtraction. This interpretation follows the sum-of-products expansion and is not a change of the drawn sign. The underbrace has ordinary powers where divided powers would be needed for the usual identity; no corrective parentheses have been added. Gamma’s subscript is a|alpha, though X would fit the previous page. The ideal-generation statement is read as idéal, not module. The unfinished margin expression is u(x. OPS. precedes a test on scalar multiples. The page bears 334.',hand=['Continuation of a product may be drawn as one horizontal dash. In this page every displayed first-to-last product uses that convention; H regularly replaces it by dots, C leaves dashes.','A small ring-shaped a/alpha can be unlike X even when the mathematical index suggests X (middle gamma subscript).','Underbraces and upright equals carry placement information; H sometimes moves their contents into the main equality.'],notation=[('single dash between factors','Written continuation stroke; left unchanged in TeX and interpreted as a product continuation in notes.'),('J subset A, K subset B','Cup-shaped signs between rows express inclusion, not check accents.'),('OPS.','Author’s conspicuous note introducing a scalar-multiple test; not expanded.')],abbr=[('pd.','puissances divisées'),('ts','tous (probable)')],checks=[check('333-text-reduction','Sum, monomial and ideal-generator reductions read as working claims, not a completed proof.'),check('333-note-product-dashes','The expansion of gamma^q(sum xi_i) uses products of gamma^{q_i}(xi_i); this identifies the connecting dashes as product continuations.','used and rechecked in this run'),check('333-text-underbrace','Ordinary-power notation in the underbrace retained; the standard divided-power identity is not silently substituted.')],unresolved=[r'sommants|sommands',r'overwritten first right subscript *|q_1',r'gamma subscript a|alpha',r'criterion introduction Downarrow|Si'])
